    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0207" n="195" xml:id="pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/2834: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-11T12:00:00+02:00">May 11,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received May 11—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1293. My number 1287, May 10, midnight. In announcing the refusal of the German
                    Foreign Office to accept the Dutch and Belgian notes of protest a DNB<anchor
                        n="58" xml:id="d143-f1"/> report published in this morning’s press describes
                    these communications as the “height of impudence, shamelessness and stupidity”
                    and characterizes the Dutch and Belgian mention of an invasion of their
                    countries as being “childish” in view of Ribbentrop’s statement of yesterday.
                    According to DNB the Dutch Minister and the Belgian Ambassador have been
                    requested to ask for their passports “in the usual proper form.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d143-f1" n="58" xml:id="d143-f1-content">
                <p>Deutsches Nachrichten Büro, German news agency.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
